# Anchored on purpose. A bare `assets` matches at ANY depth, which also
# swallowed `_app/immutable/assets/` — the built CSS and the two Inter woff2
# files. That is invisible locally but breaks a `gh-pages` branch deploy, where
# the publisher runs `git add .` and silently drops those files, leaving a live
# site with no styles and no fonts. Only the repo-root `assets/` is meant here.
/assets

web/favicon.png
compress-project.js
# package.json
# postcss.config.js
# svelte.config.js
# tailwing.config.js
# tsconfig.json
# vite.config.ts

# `package-lock.json` is deliberately NOT ignored: CI installs with `npm ci`,
# which requires a committed lockfile, and reproducible installs need it.
# (Removing it from here is also what unblocked the deploy workflow, which
# failed with "Dependencies lock file is not found".)

# `.github/` is ignored by GitHub's own scaffold default, so the workflows dir
# needs an explicit exception or Pages never runs. These negations must come
# AFTER the ignore line below — later rules win, and a trailing bare `.github`
# would silently re-ignore any NEW file added under `.github/workflows/`.
.github
!.github/
!.github/workflows/